  {
    "id": "official-azure-fang",
    "source": "authoring/scenarios/export-official-azure-fang-rev2.json",
    "revision": "REV2",
    "name": "Operation Azure Fang",
    "location": "The Pacific Northwest",
    "overview": "Golden light glitters in bright speckles across the surface of a deep blue lake. A rain of debris suddenly falls, shattering the peaceful scene and sending waves crashing in all directions. The valuable wreckage gradually sinks to the bottom as the waves above it settle. Quiet solitude returns to the lake, until the day the booming roars of warfare disturb its peace once more.\n\nSecure the supply crates (Objective tokens) in and around the lake. Supply crates must be picked up and carried by a unit in order to control them.",
    "objectives": "Neutral Objective tokens are treated as “supply crates” in this scenario and can be picked up and transported by units. At the end of each Phase, earn 5 VP for each supply crate held by your units.\n\n• When a unit ends its action on (not adjacent to) a hex containing a supply crate, that unit can pick up the supply crate. When picked up, remove the supply crate from the game board and place it on the appropriate unit card.\n\n• Each unit may only carry one supply crate at a time.\n\n• Units may drop supply crates at any time. When dropped, place the supply crate’s token on the hex where the unit is currently located. Supply crates that have been dropped are no longer under that player’s control.\n\n• When a unit Dashes, or is Pushed or Pulled, it automatically drops any supply crates it is carrying onto the hex where it is positioned when the action occurs.\n\n• When a unit is defeated, any supply crates it was carrying are dropped in the hex where it was defeated. The unit is then removed from the game board.",
    "palette": "jungle",
